  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "correction; revision; adjustment; calibration",
      "explanation": "The act of making corrections or adjustments to fix errors or improve accuracy. Used in technical, budgetary, and everyday contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "18527_hosei_ex1",
      "japanese": "{色|いろ}を{補正|ほせい}する。",
      "english": "To correct the color.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18527_hosei_ex2",
      "japanese": "{補正|ほせい}{予算|よさん}が{国会|こっかい}で{可決|かけつ}された。",
      "english": "The supplementary budget was passed in the Diet.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18527_hosei_ex3",
      "japanese": "カメラの{露出|ろしゅつ}{補正|ほせい}を{調整|ちょうせい}して、{写真|しゃしん}の{明|あか}るさを{変|か}えた。",
      "english": "I adjusted the camera's exposure compensation to change the brightness of the photo.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Very common in several domains. In government: {補正|ほせい}{予算|よさん} (supplementary budget — an additional budget passed after the initial annual budget). In photography: {露出|ろしゅつ}{補正|ほせい} (exposure compensation). In fashion/undergarments: {補正|ほせい}{下着|したぎ} (shapewear, corrective underwear). In data: データの{補正|ほせい} (data correction). Different from {修正|しゅうせい} (correction/amendment), which implies fixing something wrong; {補正|ほせい} emphasizes supplementing or adjusting to improve.",
